{:category :llm-tool
 :description
 [[:p [:b "Nautilos"]
   " is a CLI/" [:wbr] "MCP server/" [:wbr] "skill/" [:wbr]
   "plugin for coding harnesses, improving nREPL interaction."]
  [:p
   "I noticed three persistent issues with how coding harnesses use REPL-y languages:"]
  [:ul
   [:li
    "Running one-off commands repeatedly, with ever-growing state recreated every time."]
   [:li
    "Inability to maintain state with servers that scope it to the connection, due to lack of
    persistence between commands."]
   [:li "Starting a REPL via " [:code "tmux"]
    ", typically leaving a trail of abandoned but still-running sessions behind as it goes."]]
  [:p
   "Nautilos is a small (~1-2MB depending on platform/" [:wbr]
   "architecture), native, Janet binary for macOS/Linux
    that opens a connection to any nREPL server as a daemon, maintaining the connection between commands."]
  [:p
   "An LLM can then issue commands as their preferred single CLI calls, receiving each response as a single
    JSON object, including support for lookups/"
   [:wbr]
   "completions to allow for exploring the codebase/" [:wbr]
   "library
    functions."]
  [:p
   "Obviously the command will work just fine if issued by a human too, the response is just tailored for
    agents. You could maybe pipe it through "
   [:code "jq"] " or something."]]
